From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sigivb72-netizen <vergilx63@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:25:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] podot: core: in-process instances (sequential Main
 relaunch in one process)

Platforms that cannot spawn processes (the iPadOS editor) can enable
in-process instances: OS::create_instance() then queues the arguments, and
the platform main loop fully cleans up Main and sets it up again with them.

- OS: instance queue, session data surviving relaunches, logger scope.
- StringName: optionally keep the entries of static StringNames (SNAME)
  alive across cleanup, so they don't dangle after a relaunch.
- Main: reset file-scope state before a repeated setup.
- CompositeLogger: allow dropping loggers added by Main.
- linuxbsd: honor GODOT_IN_PROCESS_INSTANCES=1 to test the flow on desktop.
